  "interpretation": "<p><strong data-start=\"65\" data-end=\"72\">RDW</strong> measures the <strong data-start=\"86\" data-end=\"122\">variation in size (anisocytosis)</strong> of red blood cells (RBCs). It helps identify <strong data-start=\"168\" data-end=\"202\">mixed or early types of anemia</strong> by showing whether RBCs are all the same size or widely varied.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>RDW Result</th>\n<th>Interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal RDW</strong></td>\n<td>RBCs are mostly uniform in size. Suggests a <strong>single type of anemia</strong> or normal erythropoiesis.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High RDW</strong></td>\n<td>RBCs vary significantly in size (<strong>anisocytosis</strong>). Suggests <strong>mixed or evolving anemia</strong>, including:</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"974\" data-end=\"1026\">\n<p data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"1026\">Iron deficiency anemia (especially early stages)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1063\">\n<p data-start=\"1029\" data-end=\"1063\">Vitamin B12 or folate deficiency</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1064\" data-end=\"1112\">\n<p data-start=\"1066\" data-end=\"1112\">Recent blood transfusion (mixed populations)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1113\" data-end=\"1172\">\n<p data-start=\"1115\" data-end=\"1172\">Sickle cell disease or thalassemia with iron deficiency</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1248\">\n<p data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1248\">Recovery phase of anemia (new large cells mixed with older small cells)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>RDW</th>\n<th>MCV</th>\n<th>Likely Interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>Iron deficiency anemia, mixed thalassemia and iron deficiency</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Normal</td>\n<td>Early nutritional anemia, mixed causes (e.g., B12 and iron deficiency)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Vitamin B12 or folate deficiency, immune hemolytic anemia</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Normal</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>Thalassemia trait, anemia of chronic disease</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Normal</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Liver disease, alcoholism, or some macrocytic anemias</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p data-start=\"1809\" data-end=\"1827\"><strong data-start=\"1813\" data-end=\"1827\">Key Points</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1829\" data-end=\"2088\">\n<li data-start=\"1829\" data-end=\"1889\">\n<p data-start=\"1831\" data-end=\"1889\">RDW is <strong data-start=\"1838\" data-end=\"1862\">not diagnostic alone</strong>; it's a supporting marker.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1890\" data-end=\"2088\">\n<p data-start=\"1892\" data-end=\"2088\">It is especially useful for <strong data-start=\"1920\" data-end=\"1991\">distinguishing between iron deficiency anemia and thalassemia trait</strong>, both of which may have microcytosis (low MCV), but only iron deficiency shows <strong data-start=\"2071\" data-end=\"2087\">elevated RDW</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
